      "content": "That's a decent start, it's definitely professional. But looking at our internal tracker, the \"urgency score\" for this draft is actually quite low. It feels a bit too soft given how fast the bleaching is actually moving. \n\nCan you try another version? I need you to beef up that sense of urgency so the score is higher, but—and I really want to emphasize this—don't just repeat the same words over and over. If the email reads like a list of buzzwords, the board will reject it immediately. Just make the stakes feel more \"immediate\" and \"urgent\" through the writing itself, while still keeping that scientific credibility we talked about.",
